# A widget whose plain pair a tuple pattern binds, taking a building `if`'s late plain
# result written below it, where the `if`'s arm gives what its own widget gives (Semantics
# ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles": any line may use any name the block binds; Type
# System ch. 2: a tuple pattern takes a plain pair apart). Over an `if` whose arms give
# values of their own the same lines lower (sem-ch04-late-value-above-taker-result-tuple:
# the choice is computed in the build). Reaches `DeferredLine`'s refusal "a line that
# takes a late result at its build, above the line that gives it, and gives a plain result
# of its own that no name binds" on prismc-fd1.
# Written by Claude (sweep-7, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Pair: fn Nat -> @((Nat, Nat))
fn @Pair k:
    Ui.Label($text=$"pair {k}")
    @ ((k, k + 1))

@Seven: @Nat
@Seven:
    Ui.Label($text=$"seven")
    @ 7

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    ((a, b)) <- @Pair n                                                # 0
    Ui.Label($text=$"{a} {b}")                                        # 1
    n <- if loud:
        k <- @Seven                                                    # 2
        @ k
    else:
        @ 20
